Package: slurmpilot
Title: Auto-Profiling 'SLURM' HPC Orchestration and 'Shiny' Offloading
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Marcus",
        family = "Harris",
        role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
        email = "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com"
    )
Description: Eliminates manual 'SLURM' scripting, blind memory and walltime
    guessing, and 'Shiny' server freezes for compute-heavy R workflows. Runs
    empirical micro-pilot replications in isolated child processes to measure
    true peak resident memory and runtime distributions, computes optimal
    'SLURM' array chunking (including Longest Processing Time load balancing)
    and resource flags, audits closures and globals before staging, scans
    project environments to emit reproducible 'Apptainer' container recipes
    and batch scripts, orchestrates single-stage and multi-stage dependent
    job DAGs over remote 'SSH'/'SLURM' or local parallel mock-'SLURM' with
    atomic SHA-256 checkpoints, independent parallel random-number streams,
    adaptive surgical retries, and post-mortem efficiency auditing, and
    provides non-blocking 'bslib'/'Shiny' telemetry modules.
